  "notes": "N-CORPE has a single fund, so it is recorded once as governmental (the statement of activities splits charges for services 1,419,211.44 and expenses 771,589.97 into a 'business-type' land operations column, but that is the same money as the rents, reimbursements, sale of assets, Labor 367,218.50 and Equipment rent 8,973.56 in the governmental fund statement and the location schedule); business_type and reported_totals.business-type are null. Basis: modified cash. Receipts and disbursements come from the Statements of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balance (p5). Other financing on p5 (capital contributions 5,830,000.00 + debt service (7,129,570.30) + sale of assets 7,600.00) prints a net total of (1,291,970.30); the debt service 7,129,570.30 is moved to disbursements (outside_printed_total, debt service principal with review; principal and interest are not split on the cash statement, the p2/p7 interest expense 1,296,430.46 is accrual), so other_financing is 5,837,600.00 (capital contributions + sale of assets, computed). 'Other' receipts 379,850.65 is categorized reimbursements/refunds with review (utilities reimbursement is 76% of it per pp6-7). Balance sheet uses the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, governmental activities column, the only column); the governmental funds balance sheet (p4) shows total 335,697.30 used for ending_cash (cash 328,100.38 plus restricted cash 7,596.92). The p2 statement of activities shows net position split into governmental/business-type columns (26,802,351.01 / 2,317,807.17); not used. Detail: the Revenues and Expenditures by Location schedule (pp6-7) is recorded from its Total column only (the four NRD location columns are cost-share splits, not functions); it is on a different basis than p5 (includes depreciation, interest income netted in expenditures, revenue total 2,682,769.78 incl. Grant Revenue and gains) so it does not tie to p5. Interest income and dividends are negative expenditure lines to tie to the printed 'Expenditures net of interest income' 3,732,283.83. 2024 columns ignored. Read pages 1-7 of 7."
